# SIS Demo — Deployment Hostnames

Production runs behind **two public hostnames** (replace the examples with your own DNS — e.g. the original reference deployment used `sis.skylarbarnes.com` / `sis-api.skylarbarnes.com`):

| Service | Example CNAME / public URL |
|---------|---------------------------|
| **Web UI** | `https://sis.YOUR-DOMAIN.com` |
| **API** | `https://sis-api.YOUR-DOMAIN.com` |

Use the same pair consistently in `.env`, Okta, SAML, CORS, and client API config:

- Set `APP_URL=https://sis.YOUR-DOMAIN.com`
- Set `API_PUBLIC_URL=https://sis-api.YOUR-DOMAIN.com`
- Set `VITE_API_URL=https://sis-api.YOUR-DOMAIN.com` (web app)
- SAML Audience URI / SP Entity ID: `https://sis-api.YOUR-DOMAIN.com/auth/saml/metadata`
- SAML ACS (Single sign-on URL): `https://sis-api.YOUR-DOMAIN.com/auth/saml/callback`

Do not use `localhost` for SAML issuer/audience in production. Local ports (3010 API, 5173 web) are for reverse-proxy upstream only.
